          "fragments": [
            {
              "scan": "s119",
              "printed_page": "45",
              "text": "for a sacred convocation, a reminder of the exodus from Egypt.",
              "page_start": false
            }
          ],
          "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/vattitten_lanu_hashem"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 3,
          "fragments": [
            {
              "scan": "s121",
              "printed_page": "46",
              "text": "Our God and God of our fathers, may there rise and come and arrive and appear and be favourably received and be heard and considered and remain in memory before Thee, our remembrance and our consideration and the memory of our fathers and the memory of the anointed, the son of David, Thy servant, and the memory of Jerusalem the Holy City, and the memory of all Thy people, the House of Israel, for deliverance and for happiness, for favour and for grace and for compassion, for life and for peace on this Day of Remembrance. Remember us, O Lord our God, on it for happiness, consider us on it for blessing and help us on it unto life, and through the word of salvation and compassion, spare us and be gracious unto us have compassion upon us, and help us, for towards Thee our eyes are turned, for Thou O God, art a gracious and merciful King.",
              "page_start": true
            }
          ],
          "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/qedushat_hayom/yaaleh_veyavo",
          "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yaaleh_veyavo"
        },
        {
          "paragraph": 4,
          "fragments": [
            {
              "scan": "s121",
              "printed_page": "46",
              "text": "Our God and God of our fathers, reign over the whole world in Thy glory and rise above the whole earth in Thy grandeur. Shine forth in the exalted beauty of Thy might upon all the inhabitants of the territory of Thine earth so that every creature may recognize that Thou hast created it and that every form may understand that Thou hast formed it and all with breath in the nostrils may say: The Lord, the God of Israel, is King and His Kingdom rules over all.",
              "page_start": false
            }
          ],
          "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/silent_amidah/qedushat_hayom/melokh",
          "source": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/melokh_al_kol_haolam"
        },
        {
